@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Claude Code code intelligence — seeded plugins, enabled per binary, no install prompt

' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
'
' ── HOW THE SEED IS BUILT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ARG CLAUDE_PLUGIN_SEED=/opt/proveo/claude-plugins, exported to the image as
' ENV CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_SEED_DIR so it is valid for whatever HOME a run uses.
'
' The build RUN drives the real `claude` CLI inside a THROWAWAY home:
'   HOME=/tmp/claude-build
'   DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1
'   CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1
'   CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR="${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_SEED}"
' then `claude plugin marketplace add anthropics/claude-plugins-official` and
' `claude plugin install <p>@claude-plugins-official` for each of:
'   typescript-lsp pyright-lsp gopls-lsp rust-analyzer-lsp clangd-lsp
'   jdtls-lsp lua-lsp
' It asserts `known_marketplaces.json` and
' `cache/claude-plugins-official/typescript-lsp` exist, then removes
' /tmp/claude-build. The list is pinned to `_claude_lsp_plugins` in
' packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh by internal/contract.
'
' THE SEED IS chmod -R a+rwX — WORLD-WRITABLE, deliberately. Claude Code drops
' `.in_use/<pid>` markers BESIDE a loaded plugin, and the runtime uid is the
' operator's rather than the baked 1000, so a read-only tree would fail those
' writes. They land in the container's own writable layer and never persist.
'
' WHY ANY OF THIS EXISTS. Claude Code offers to install an official `*-lsp`
' plugin whenever it finds that plugin's language-server binary on PATH with the
' plugin absent — "If you already have a language server installed, Claude may
' prompt you to install the corresponding plugin when you open a project"
' (Discover and install plugins, Code intelligence). This image BAKES the
' binaries, so every session opened with an install prompt for a plugin nobody
' asked for, and a sandbox home could never keep the answer. The documented
' remedy is a seed: a read-only mirror of ~/.claude/plugins that Claude Code
' reads in place — marketplace registration and plugin caches, no network at run
' time.
'
' ── THE RULE IS THE BINARY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Knobs: PROVEO_CLAUDE_LSP_PLUGINS=off · CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_SEED_DIR (image-set).
'
' The image seeds the official `*-lsp` plugins so Claude Code stops offering to
' install them; the entrypoint decides which are ON. An official plugin is
' enabled exactly when its language server is on PATH after provisioning.
' Present binary + absent plugin is what prompts; present plugin + absent
' binary is an "Executable not found" error in /plugin. Enabling per binary
' produces neither. proveo-lsp then declares only the languages no enabled
' official plugin already covers, so no extension has two servers racing.
' Pinned to the Dockerfile's install list by internal/contract.
'
' Settings are MERGED into the agent's user file: it is the operator's, an
' explicit `false` there is respected, and the run is idempotent.
' PROVEO_CLAUDE_LSP_OFFICIAL is exported as the set configure_claude_lsp must
' leave alone.
'
' ── THE SEED IS NOT ENOUGH: CLAUDE CODE NEEDS ITS OWN RECORDS ──────────────
' Two files are written into the home — plugins/installed_plugins.json and
' plugins/known_marketplaces.json — pointing at the seed. Measured on 2.1.251
' (2026-09-01): with the seed alone, startup logs "Skipping orphaned
' enabledPlugins entry … marketplace not registered" and loads 0 plugins; with
' the records present it lists the plugin enabled with its LSP server. The seed
' is where the files live; the records are how Claude Code finds them. Existing
' entries in either file are the operator's and are never overwritten.

node "Image build — defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile" as BUILD <<host>> {
  component "language servers on PATH\n""typescript-language-server"" · ""pyright-langserver"" · …" as BIN <<app>>
  component "plugin seed — ""/opt/proveo/claude-plugins""\n""known_marketplaces.json"" · ""marketplaces/"" · ""cache/""" as SEED <<db>>
}
cloud "anthropics/claude-plugins-official\n(clone once, at build)" as MKT <<cloud>>

node "Seed step — ""proveo_seed claudecode""" as RUN <<host>> {
  component "provision servers for the\nworkspace's languages" as PROV <<app>>
  component "**enable** — ""proveo_enable_claude_lsp_plugins""\nplugin ON ⇔ its binary is on PATH" as EN <<app>>
  component "**proveo-lsp** — ""configure_claude_lsp""\nthe languages no official plugin covers" as OWN <<app>>
}

component "Claude Code\n""CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_SEED_DIR""" as CC <<app>>
component "install prompt\n'language server found — install its plugin?'" as PROMPT <<error>>

MKT   ARROW_CLOUD SEED : ""claude plugin marketplace add"" ·\n""claude plugin install <p>@claude-plugins-official""
SEED  ARROW_MAIN CC : read in place, read-only,\nno network at run time
BIN   ARROW_ERROR PROMPT : binary present + plugin absent\nis what used to prompt
EN    ARROW_MAIN CC : install + marketplace records → the seed;\n""enabledPlugins[…] = true"" — all merged, never overwritten
PROV  ARROW_MAIN EN
EN    ARROW_MAIN OWN : ""PROVEO_CLAUDE_LSP_OFFICIAL"" — languages to leave alone
OWN   ARROW_MAIN CC : ""~/.claude/skills/proveo-lsp/.lsp.json""
CC    ARROW_OPTIONAL PROMPT : never — every present\nbinary has its plugin

note bottom of SEED
  **The seed holds the files; the home holds the records.**
  Measured on 2.1.251: the seed alone is "marketplace not
  registered", 0 plugins. So the seed step writes
  ""installed_plugins.json"" and ""known_marketplaces.json""
  into the run's HOME pointing here. Build: 16 s, 9.9 MB.
end note

note left of SEED
  **World-writable, and for a specific reason.**
  Claude Code drops an ""\.in_use/<pid>"" marker
  beside a loaded plugin, and the runtime uid is
  the operator's, not 1000 — so the seed is
  ""chmod -R a+rwX"" and the writes stay in-layer.
end note

note right of EN
  **The binary decides, not the list.** Present binary and
  absent plugin prompts; present plugin and absent binary
  is "Executable not found" in ""/plugin"". Enabling per
  binary, after provisioning, produces neither. An explicit
  ""false"" the operator wrote is left alone.
end note

note bottom of OWN
  **One server per extension.** Two enabled servers on one
  extension means the second never starts and ""/plugin""
  warns. proveo-lsp keeps bash, yaml, json, docker, html,
  css, markdown, toml, terraform, plantuml, zig, nix, ruby,
  kotlin — and yields typescript, python, go, rust, cpp,
  java, lua to the official plugins when they are on.
end note

note left of BUILD
  **kotlin-lsp is not seeded.** It expects a ""kotlin-lsp""
  binary; this floor provisions fwcd's
  ""kotlin-language-server"", which proveo-lsp drives. A
  seeded plugin that can never find its binary would only
  add an error row. ""internal/contract"" pins seed ⇔ table.
end note
@enduml
